  "part_of_speech": "noun, suru verb, no-adjective",
  "gloss": "attached; affiliated; accessory",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "attached; affiliated; accessory",
      "explanation": "Connected to or part of a larger organization, product, or institution. Common in school names ({付属|ふぞく}{小学校|しょうがっこう}) and product accessories ({付属品|ふぞくひん})."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "27518_fuzoku_ex1",
      "japanese": "{付属|ふぞく}のケーブルを{使|つか}ってください。",
      "english": "Please use the included cable.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "27518_fuzoku_ex2",
      "japanese": "{息子|むすこ}は{大学|だいがく}{付属|ふぞく}の{中学校|ちゅうがっこう}に{通|かよ}っている。",
      "english": "My son attends a middle school affiliated with a university.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "27518_fuzoku_ex3",
      "japanese": "{説明書|せつめいしょ}は{箱|はこ}に{付属|ふぞく}しているので{確認|かくにん}してください。",
      "english": "The manual comes with the box, so please check it.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "The more common modern spelling of {附属|ふぞく}; the two are interchangeable in meaning. Used both as a noun-modifier (X{付属|ふぞく}Y = Y attached to X) and as a する verb meaning 'to be attached to / come with'.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {大学|だいがく}{付属|ふぞく}{病院|びょういん}: university-affiliated hospital\n- {付属品|ふぞくひん}: accessories, included parts\n- {付属|ふぞく}している: is attached / comes included\n- {付属|ふぞく}{書類|しょるい}: attached documents\n\nWRITING:\nIn educational and institutional names (e.g. {筑波大学|つくばだいがく}{附属|ふぞく}{高校|こうこう}), the older form {附属|ふぞく} is still standard. In everyday writing about product accessories, {付属|ふぞく} dominates.",
